diff --git a/packages/core/session/README.md b/packages/core/session/README.md
index 178dc708..b46e8056 100644
--- a/packages/core/session/README.md
+++ b/packages/core/session/README.md
@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@ English | [中文](README.zh.md)
 
 `dsh-session` records every model-visible fact in an append-only session log and derives model history from that record. Consumers can inspect, replay, fork, and flush sessions while preserving historical events; compaction hides superseded entries from the active conversation without deleting them. Sessions remain in memory unless a persistence backend is added, and durability checkpoints wait for configured backends. Choose this package wherever an agent needs a reconstructable session record; it does not call models.
 
+`beginRetirement(id)` reserves one ID before asynchronous closure. The Agent registry must first claim the idle owner. Only the supplied finalizer may append while closing; create and enter remain blocked. Closing awaits returned `session/disposed` promises. Releasing is allowed only before closing; once closing begins, the ID stays reserved until Host restart. Fire-and-forget listener work is outside this completion promise.
+
